# Shell scripts are stored and checked out with LF, always.
#
# Development happens on Windows and CI runs on Linux. Today the scripts are
# stored correctly only because this machine has core.autocrlf=true, which is a
# per-clone setting and not a property of the repository. A clone without it
# would commit CRLF, and bash on the runner answers a CRLF shebang with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — a failure that names the
# interpreter rather than the line endings and costs an hour to read.
#
# Deliberately scoped to *.sh rather than a repository-wide `* text=auto`.
# Normalising everything would rewrite line endings across the whole tree in
# one commit, which is a separate decision with its own review cost.
*.sh text eol=lf
